<title>TURKEY: Turkish Jan-May trade deficit falls.</title>
<headline>Turkish Jan-May trade deficit falls.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's foreign trade deficit fell 2.7 percent to $7.83 billion in the first five months of this year over the same 1996 period, the State Institute of Statistics said.</p>
<p>It said exports rose 9.4 percent to $9.79 billion and imports 3.6 percent to $17.62 billion in January-May.</p>
</text>
